wlcs v1.8.1: the text-input tests that map a window attach its buffer before the compositor's initial configure is acknowledged.

Same defect as 0001, 0002 and 0003, in tests/text_input_v3_with_input_method_v2.cpp: text_input_does_not_enter_non_grabbing_popup,
text_input_enters_grabbing_popup and text_input_enters_parent_surface_after_child_destroyed create an xdg_surface and
its role object and attach a buffer to it (the parent window, the popup or the child toplevel) without the initial
commit and without acknowledging the configure that answers it. That is xdg_surface.unconfigured_buffer, so a
compositor that enforces the rule (Smithay does) closed the connection before the test asked the text input anything.
The tests now commit without a buffer and acknowledge the configure first, as the patches for the popup and toplevel
fixtures do. Every expectation of the tests is unchanged.

Applied by scripts/wlcs.sh with `git apply`; drop it when wlcs fixes the tests upstream.

diff --git a/tests/text_input_v3_with_input_method_v2.cpp b/tests/text_input_v3_with_input_method_v2.cpp
index 2142cea..5e6ae04 100644
--- a/tests/text_input_v3_with_input_method_v2.cpp
+++ b/tests/text_input_v3_with_input_method_v2.cpp
@@ -34,6 +34,31 @@
 
 using namespace testing;
 
+namespace
+{
+// Commits the surface without a buffer and acknowledges the compositor's answer, the initial configure. Only then
+// may a buffer be attached (xdg_surface.unconfigured_buffer).
+void ack_initial_configure(wlcs::Client& client, wlcs::Surface& surface, wlcs::XdgSurfaceStable& xdg_shell_surface)
+{
+    bool configured = false;
+    ON_CALL(xdg_shell_surface, configure)
+        .WillByDefault(
+            [&configured, raw = static_cast<xdg_surface*>(xdg_shell_surface)](uint32_t serial)
+            {
+                xdg_surface_ack_configure(raw, serial);
+                configured = true;
+            });
+    wl_surface_commit(surface);
+    client.dispatch_until([&configured]() { return configured; });
+    ON_CALL(xdg_shell_surface, configure)
+        .WillByDefault(
+            [raw = static_cast<xdg_surface*>(xdg_shell_surface)](uint32_t serial)
+            {
+                xdg_surface_ack_configure(raw, serial);
+            });
+}
+}
+
